# Optional environment variables (set them in your shell; this file is documentation only).
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.company:8080      corporate proxy for /download
# SSL_CERT_FILE=C:\path\company-root-ca.pem  only if the OS trust store is not enough
# LMA_DATA_DIR=D:\lma-data                   where models, index, memory and snapshots are stored
# LMA_CONFIG_DIR=C:\path\to\config           alternative config folder
# LMA_LLAMA_SERVER=C:\tools\llama\llama-server.exe   use an existing/approved llama.cpp build
# LMA_MAIA_URL=http://localhost:7782/mcp     only for tests/test_maia_live.py
# Secrets never go into config files: use `/config secret NAME` (Windows Credential Manager)
# and reference them as keyring:NAME, or env:NAME for environment variables.
